.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-gpg-list 1  "git-gpg-list " 
.SH NAME
git\-gpg\-list \- List all tracked files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-gpg list\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List all tracked files
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
Prints every file tracked in .git\-gpg/tracked.json. Tracking records
intent only: whether the plaintext or its .secret ciphertext currently
exists on disk is not checked.

EXAMPLES
  $ git\-gpg list
